flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the connection to the board behaves
  accDescr: At the start, the integration waits three seconds for the board at most and then loads anyway, reading the board every 2 seconds. With the first valid realtime message, darts arrive at once and a read only reconciles every 30 seconds, every 10 seconds with Board Manager 2. When the realtime connection drops, the integration reads every 2 seconds again and reconnects after 1, 2, 4 up to 60 seconds, each wait up to a fifth shorter. Two missed reads in a row keep the last values; the third makes the board entities unavailable, and after about ten the board is asked every 15 seconds. Its first answer brings back fast polling and an immediate reconnect.
  START(["Home Assistant starts:<br/>waits 3 s for the board at most,<br/>then loads anyway"]) --> FAST["Fast polling:<br/>a read every 2 s"]
  FAST -- "first valid<br/>realtime message" --> REALTIME["Realtime: every dart at once,<br/>a read to reconcile every 30 s,<br/>10 s with Board Manager 2"]
  REALTIME -- "the connection drops" --> RETRY["Fast polling at once,<br/>reconnect after 1, 2, 4 … 60 s,<br/>each wait up to a fifth shorter"]
  RETRY -- "reconnected" --> REALTIME
  RETRY -- "the board does<br/>not answer" --> HICCUP["1 or 2 missed reads:<br/>the last values stay"]
  HICCUP -- "the third missed read" --> UNAVAILABLE["The board entities<br/>are unavailable"]
  UNAVAILABLE -- "about ten<br/>missed reads" --> AWAY["Board away:<br/>a read every 15 s"]
  AWAY -- "the first answer" --> BACK["Fast polling again,<br/>reconnect right away"]
  BACK --> REALTIME
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef warn fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
  class REALTIME done
  class UNAVAILABLE,AWAY warn
